cargo-audit (vulnerabilities)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-16T12:45:30.6576674Z {"database":{"advisory-count":1509,"last-commit":"02e2517f457a359fc6d3440ea4560c8ea188fee8","last-updated":"2026-11-15T10:59:21+01:00"},"lockfile":{"dependency-count":138},"settings":{"target_arch":[],"target_os":[],"severity":null,"ignore":[],"informational_warnings":["unmaintained","unsound","notice"]},"vulnerabilities":{"found":false,"count":0,"list":[]},"warnings":{"unmaintained":[{"kind":"unmaintained","package":{"name":"pin-utils","version":"0.1.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"13bee6c73da26345c729282832b60b0363cf3dd9f4bfd81d8551b7a1c889a113","replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0441","package":"pin-utils","title":"`pin-utils` is unmaintained","description":"The [upstream repository] was archived on October 1, 2026, after the\nrelease of version 0.1.1.\n\nFor local pinning, replace `pin_mut!` with [`core::pin::pin!`], available\nsince Rust 1.68. For pin projection, replace `unsafe_pinned!` and\n`unsafe_unpinned!` with [`pin-project`] or [`pin-project-lite`].\n\n[upstream repository]: https://github.com/rust-lang/pin-utils\n[`core::pin::pin!`]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/core/pin/macro.pin.html\n[`pin-project`]: https://crates.io/crates/pin-project\n[`pin-project-lite`]: https://crates.io/crates/pin-project-lite","date":"2026-10-01","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":"unmaintained","references":["https://github.com/rustsec/advisory-db/issues/3314"],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/rust-lang/team/pull/2787","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[],"unaffected":[]}},{"kind":"unmaintained","package":{"name":"serial","version":"0.4.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"a1237a96570fc377c13baa1b88c7589ab66edced652e43ffb17088f003db3e86","dependencies":[{"name":"serial-core","version":"0.4.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"serial-unix","version":"0.4.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"serial-windows","version":"0.4.0","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2017-0008","package":"serial","title":"`serial` crate is unmaintained","description":"The [`serial`](https://crates.io/crates/serial) crate is no longer maintained.\n\nLast release was on 2017-07-02.\n\n## Possible alternatives\n\nConsider using an alternative, for instance the blocking librarys:\n\n- [serial2](https://crates.io/crates/serial2)\n- [serialport](https://crates.io/crates/serialport)\n\nor async alternatives:\n\n- [mio-serial](https://crates.io/crates/mio-serial)\n- [tokio-serial](https://crates.io/crates/tokio-serial)","date":"2017-07-02","aliases":[],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":[],"cvss":null,"informational":"unmaintained","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/dcuddeback/serial-rs/issues/71","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":null,"versions":{"patched":[],"unaffected":[]}}],"unsound":[{"kind":"unsound","package":{"name":"rustix","version":"1.1.5","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index","checksum":"891efababe418670775f199f0d233d84843c227a0949a883ce15b37c78d6629d","dependencies":[{"name":"bitflags","version":"2.13.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"errno","version":"0.3.14","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"libc","version":"0.2.190","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"linux-raw-sys","version":"0.12.1","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"},{"name":"windows-sys","version":"0.61.2","source":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"}],"replace":null},"advisory":{"id":"RUSTSEC-2026-0486","package":"rustix","title":"xattr functions mark unwritten bytes as initialized when given a zero-length buffer","description":"The extended-attribute functions in `rustix::fs` (`getxattr`, `lgetxattr`, `fgetxattr`, `listxattr`, `llistxattr` and `flistxattr`) write into a `Buffer` and then mark as many bytes initialized as the system call reported. When the buffer has zero length, the operating system treats the call as a size query: it writes nothing and returns the size of the attribute value or of the name list. rustix still marked that many bytes as initialized.\n\nPassing a `Vec` whose length equals its capacity through `spare_capacity` gives such a zero-length buffer, and rustix then set the vector's length past its capacity over memory that was never written. This is undefined behavior reachable from safe code. With an empty `&mut [MaybeUninit<u8>]` the call panics instead.\n\nFrom 1.1.6 these functions return an empty result for a zero-length buffer, and new `getxattr_query`, `lgetxattr_query`, `fgetxattr_query`, `listxattr_query`, `llistxattr_query` and `flistxattr_query` functions return the size. The 0.38 series did not have the `Buffer` API and is not affected.","date":"2026-10-27","aliases":["GHSA-jh2m-fhpj-3vr7"],"related":[],"collection":"crates","categories":[],"keywords":["xattr","uninitialized-memory"],"cvss":null,"informational":"unsound","references":[],"source":null,"url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/rustix/commit/8e6aaa6713d2bb64b1fdd8c472e3a32a10a76d70","withdrawn":null,"license":"CC0-1.0","expect-deleted":false},"affected":{"arch":[],"os":[],"functions":{"rustix::fs::fgetxattr":[">=1.0.0, <1.1.6"],"rustix::fs::flistxattr":[">=1.0.0, <1.1.6"],"rustix::fs::getxattr":[">=1.0.0, <1.1.6"],"rustix::fs::lgetxattr":[">=1.0.0, <1.1.6"],"rustix::fs::listxattr":[">=1.0.0, <1.1.6"],"rustix::fs::llistxattr":[">=1.0.0, <1.1.6"]}},"versions":{"patched":[">=1.1.6"],"unaffected":["<1.0.0"]}}]}}
